      "remaining_components": [
        "The separate arbitrary-power multi-index coefficient formula in final:todd-arbitrary-power is not yet formalized."
      ],
      "proof_method": "Native PowerSeries formal differentiation of the actual quotient gives X*Tprime=(1+X)*T-T^2. Its twisted-power derivative identity yields the exact diagonal coefficient recurrence, proving all twists without assuming any tower observation. This is an alternative proof of the displayed theorem; no generic Laurent residue-substitution theorem is asserted."
    },
    {
      "statement_id": "final:F2",
      "status": "proved",
      "checked_scope": "Actual normalized formal Todd, Ahat, L, and chi_y series, defined by the native formal exponential and unit denominators, with their stated quotient identities and all displayed reconstruction formulas. Both exponential recoveries are proved. The Ahat-only square root exists uniquely with constant term 2 and reconstructs the actual Todd quotient. The chi affine rescaling has both inverse directions for fixed y != -1 over every characteristic-zero field, degenerates to 1+X at y=-1, and has an explicit normalized noninjectivity counterexample there. All stated standard formulas and unit inversion are also proved over arbitrary commutative Q-algebras, including zero divisors, with the exact IsUnit(1+y) condition. The parameter-polynomial case is instantiated in native Localization.Away(1+Polynomial.X), giving the actual Q[y,(1+y)^-1] inverse domain.",
